Package: braincell-mcp
Version: @VERSION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Depends: python3 (>= @PYMIN@), python3 (<< @PYMAX@), python3-venv
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Maintainer: Karl Toussaint (kt2saint) <kt2saint.create@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/kt2saint-sec/braincell-mcp
Description: Local-first persistent-memory MCP server (SQLite + hybrid search)
 braincell-mcp is a standalone MCP (Model Context Protocol) server that gives
 coding agents cross-project working memory: per-project brains stored in a
 single SQLite file, hybrid vector + FTS5 ranking, and recall / remember /
 forget / supersede tools, plus a build & sync CLI and an optional local GUI.
 .
 The package bundles all Python dependencies as wheels and creates a private
 virtualenv under /opt/braincell-mcp at install time (no network access is
 needed during installation). The bundled binary wheels target the Python
 minor version this package was built for (see Depends).
 .
 External prerequisite (NOT packaged, not available in the Debian/Ubuntu
 archives): Ollama, running locally with an embedding model pulled
 (default: qwen3-embedding:4b). See /usr/share/doc/braincell-mcp/.
